# Place a held object: approach, release, and retreat.
#
# WHEN THIS RESULT COMES FROM THE TWIN BOUNDARY (L5), it is an aggregate of two
# cells and not one cell's answer. `cite_twin` decides every field of it, and
# the rule is per field rather than per message:
#
#   * `result` is ranked by consequence over the sides, worst first, and every
#     side is named in `detail`.
#   * `still_holding` states CUSTODY and is the logical OR over the sides the
#     goal was dispatched to - somebody is holding it. A dispatched side that
#     returned no result at all counts as holding, because unknown custody has
#     to fall on the side that makes L4 escalate rather than the side that
#     makes it open a gripper (ADR-0038 decision 5, ADR-0046).
#   * `release_pose` and `duration` are one side's MEASUREMENT. Two arms
#     produce two of them and their mean is a value neither arm produced, so L5
#     forwards the PLANT's whole - the side the operator is on (ADR-0044 clause
#     5) - and says so in `detail`. Where the plant returned no result, none is
#     forwarded and `detail` says that instead; the counterpart's number is
#     never reported under the plant's name.

geometry_msgs/PoseStamped target_pose
float64 approach_distance_m             # m
float64 retreat_distance_m              # m
bool require_holding                    # fail rather than mime a place when the
                                        # gripper reports nothing held
---
ResultCode result
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped release_pose
builtin_interfaces/Duration duration
bool still_holding                      # LAST, AND NOT SECOND AS ON `Transfer`.
                                        # Inserting a field between two existing
                                        # ones moves both, which is the
                                        # reordering `test_interface_contract.py`
                                        # names as breaking every consumer already
                                        # built against this message; appending is
                                        # the one placement it calls safe. Reading
                                        # order is worth less than that.
                                        #
                                        # Whether the arm is STILL HOLDING the
                                        # work-piece when this result is sent.
                                        # True on every failure before the
                                        # release, and false after a place that
                                        # got as far as opening the jaws.
                                        #
                                        # It exists because a place can abort
                                        # WITH THE PART IN THE GRIPPER - the
                                        # descent onto the release pose is the
                                        # motion three CI runs died in - and
                                        # this action had no field that could
                                        # say so. L4 chooses a recovery from
                                        # custody rather than from the result
                                        # code (ADR-0046): a retry begins with
                                        # MoveToHome and `Pick`'s first physical
                                        # act is to open the gripper, so a wrong
                                        # value here drops a part no planner
                                        # knows is held (ADR-0038 decision 5).
                                        #
                                        # False with SUCCESS is the ordinary
                                        # case and not a defect - a completed
                                        # place has let go.
                                        #
                                        # NOTHING HERE OPENS THE JAWS on a
                                        # failure. What to do with a held part
                                        # is a decision for a person, and this
                                        # field is how they are told there is
                                        # one to make.
---
uint8 PHASE_PLANNING=0
uint8 PHASE_APPROACHING=1
uint8 PHASE_RELEASING=2
uint8 PHASE_RETREATING=3
uint8 phase
float64 fraction_complete               # 0..1
